@* M-D3 owner ruling (U2), progress.md near-verbatim: "U2 xref expansion --
   down: +2 refs; up: -2; double-down: all; double-up: collapse to
   original." Extended by U6 to Catechism ("Catechism defaults to 2 shown
   + U2 mechanics") -- ONE component, parameterized, backing BOTH lists
   ("one component/behavior, parameterized -- never two implementations,"
   the brief's own words, the identical discipline PASSAGE-1/
   CAP-RECONCILE-1 already establish elsewhere in this popover platform).
   PassageList.razor uses this INTERNALLY for its own cross-references/
   THE SCRIPTURES/place est-dest reveal (REPLACES its retired binary
   Cap/_showAll all-or-nothing toggle); CatechismSeamSection uses it
   DIRECTLY (its own list is a plain button row, not a PassageList/
   PassageSourceUnit consumer, so it cannot go through that component --
   this one is deliberately shaped generically enough for either caller:
   a total count, a floor, a step, and a currently-shown count, nothing
   about WHAT is being shown).

   M-D4 fix round 1, P2 (owner order, 2026-08-23, verbatim: "the down/
   double down thing is really ugly and needs work. make a sensible
   decision about how to achieve what i want: the ability to show a
   little more with one click; the ability to show everything with
   another click, and the ability to undo either of those operations
   with a click"). CONTROLLER DESIGN DECISION (delegated by the owner,
   ledgered progress.md "Owner: reveal controls REDESIGN ordered"): the
   four-glyph arrow-button cluster this file used to render RETIRES
   WHOLE -- replaced by ONE quiet inline text row, house `.explorable-quiet`
   register (cursor:pointer, no ink-wash -- this control is a plain
   utility, not a popover-opening explorable target), honest counts in
   the visible label itself, STATE-ADAPTIVE:
     collapsed (Shown == Default):  more (n) &middot; all (N)
     partial (Default < Shown < Total): more (n) &middot; all (N) &middot; less
     fully expanded (Shown == Total): less
   "all (N)" is the list's own TRUE Total, always -- "the ability to show
   EVERYTHING," never a shrinking "remaining" count that would just
   duplicate what "more (n)" already says. Conditionally OMITTED (not
   merely relabeled) whenever it would be IDENTICAL to "more" -- i.e.
   whenever a single MORE click already reaches Total (`Total - Shown <=
   Step`, see ShowAll below) -- "reveal everything" is only a genuinely
   DIFFERENT action from "reveal a little more" when there is more than
   one further step to jump past; this is also what naturally handles
   MiniReaderExpand.razor's own binary Default=0/Total=1/Step=1 case
   (its own single MORE click always already IS "everything") with no
   special-casing of its own -- see that file's own usage, unchanged
   from before this redesign.

   LESS is a ONE-OP UNDO, not a plain decrement, per the owner's own
   third ask ("undo either of those operations with a click"): after
   ALL, LESS returns to the EXACT pre-ALL view (a one-deep memory,
   _preAllShown below -- not a full history stack); after MORE (or once
   that one-deep memory has already been spent), LESS steps back by
   exactly Step, floored at Default -- "repeated LESS walks home."
   _preAllShown is real, disclosed component-instance STATE (a
   deliberate, small widening of this component's own prior "fully
   stateless, Shown owned entirely by the caller" framing) -- safe by
   the SAME "freshly instantiated per popover-section resolve, never
   reused across genuinely different lists" discipline this file's own
   Shown/_shown precedent already established one layer up in every
   caller (PassageList.razor's own _shown field doc comment has the
   fuller reasoning): a caller can only ever change Shown BY calling
   ShownChanged, i.e. THROUGH this component's own click handlers, so
   there is no external mutation path that could leave _preAllShown
   stale relative to Shown.

   CONDITIONAL PRESENCE (unchanged principle, new shape): renders nothing
   at all when Total &lt;= Default (nothing to reveal, the SAME "no arrow
   at all under the cap" rule XREF-1 always followed). *@
@if (Total > Default)
{
    <div class="popover-reveal-controls">
        @if (Shown < Total)
        {
            <button type="button" class="popover-reveal-link explorable-quiet" data-testid="@MoreTestId"
                    aria-label="@(MoreLabel ?? $"Show {MoreCount} more {RevealNoun}")"
                    title="@(MoreLabel ?? $"Show {MoreCount} more {RevealNoun}")"
                    @onclick="OnMoreClick" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">@(MoreLabel ?? $"more ({MoreCount})")</button>
            @if (ShowAll)
            {
                <span class="popover-reveal-sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
                <button type="button" class="popover-reveal-link explorable-quiet" data-testid="@($"{MoreTestId}-all")"
                        aria-label="@(MoreLabel ?? $"Show all {Total} {RevealNoun}")"
                        title="@(MoreLabel ?? $"Show all {Total} {RevealNoun}")"
                        @onclick="OnAllClick" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">@(MoreLabel ?? $"all ({Total})")</button>
            }
        }
        @if (Shown > Default)
        {
            @if (Shown < Total)
            {
                <span class="popover-reveal-sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
            }
            <button type="button" class="popover-reveal-link explorable-quiet" data-testid="@CollapseTestId"
                    aria-label="@(CollapseLabel ?? $"Show fewer {RevealNoun}")"
                    title="@(CollapseLabel ?? $"Show fewer {RevealNoun}")"
                    @onclick="OnLessClick" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">@(CollapseLabel ?? "less")</button>
        }
    </div>
}

@code {
    // The list's own true total size -- never re-derived from Shown/Step,
    // always the caller's own ground truth (PassageList's own _blocks.Count,
    // CatechismSeamSection's own items.Count).
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public int Total { get; set; }

    // The floor collapsing never crosses -- the SAME number the list's own
    // initial render already shows (PassageList's existing Cap parameter,
    // CatechismSeamSection's own new 2, F2/CAP-RECONCILE-1's 2-vs-3 xrefs
    // rule) -- "never below the default," the owner's own words.
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public int Default { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public int Step { get; set; } = 2;

    // Two-way bound -- the caller owns the actual VISIBLE-COUNT state (its
    // own _shown field), this component only ever proposes the next value
    // via ShownChanged; _preAllShown below is the one piece of state this
    // component DOES now own itself (see this file's own header comment
    // for why that's safe) -- purely a UI-affordance memory, never
    // something the caller needs to know about or persist.
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public int Shown { get; set; }
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public EventCallback<int> ShownChanged { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string MoreTestId { get; set; } = "reveal-more";
    [Parameter] public string CollapseTestId { get; set; } = "reveal-collapse";
    [Parameter] public string RevealNoun { get; set; } = "entries";

    // O2 (unchanged from before this redesign): verbatim label override for
    // MiniReaderExpand.razor's own genuinely-binary case ("Read the whole
    // chapter" doesn't fit the generic "{N} more {RevealNoun}" template --
    // see that file's own comment). MoreLabel covers BOTH the "more" and
    // "all" buttons when set (ShowAll is always false in the binary case
    // that needs this override -- see this file's own header comment --
    // so only "more" ever actually renders with it in practice). Null
    // (every list-shaped caller: PassageList's own list-level Cap reveal,
    // CatechismSeamSection) keeps the generated "more (N)"/"all (N)" copy.
    [Parameter] public string? MoreLabel { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string? CollapseLabel { get; set; }

    // How many MORE would be revealed by a single MORE click -- shown IN
    // the visible label itself now (progress.md's own literal "more (2)"),
    // not just the aria-label/title the old arrow-glyph design confined it to.
    private int MoreCount => Math.Min(Step, Total - Shown);

    // "all" is a genuinely DIFFERENT action from "more" only when a single
    // MORE click would not already reach Total -- see this file's own
    // header comment for why this is a conditional-presence rule, not a
    // special case, and how it subsumes MiniReaderExpand.razor's own binary
    // usage with no caller-side change.
    private bool ShowAll => Total - Shown > Step;

    // One-deep undo memory -- see this file's own header comment for the
    // full "after ALL vs. after MORE" semantics.
    private int? _preAllShown;

    private Task OnMoreClick()
    {
        _preAllShown = null; // a NEW forward step invalidates any earlier "undo the last ALL" memory
        return ShownChanged.InvokeAsync(Math.Min(Shown + Step, Total));
    }

    private Task OnAllClick()
    {
        _preAllShown = Shown; // remember where we jumped FROM, for LESS's own one-deep undo
        return ShownChanged.InvokeAsync(Total);
    }

    private Task OnLessClick()
    {
        if (_preAllShown is int pre)
        {
            _preAllShown = null; // consumed -- ONE-deep, not a full history stack
            return ShownChanged.InvokeAsync(pre);
        }

        return ShownChanged.InvokeAsync(Math.Max(Shown - Step, Default));
    }
}
